===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|ynogh}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ġenōg||enough}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*ganōgaz||enough}} (compare {{cog|sco|eneuch}}, {{cog|fy|genôch}}, {{cog|nl|genoeg}}, {{cog|de|genug}}, {{cog|nds|(ge)noog}}, {{cog|da|nok}}, {{cog|sv|nog}}, {{cog|is|nógur}}), from {{m|gem-pro|*ganuganą}} 'to suffice' (compare {{cog|ang|ġeneah}}), or from {{m|gem-pro|*ga-}} + an unattested *''nōgaz'', probably ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂eh₂nó(n)ḱe||he has reached, attained}}, perfective of {{m|ine-pro|*h₂neḱ-||to reach}} (compare {{cog|sga|tánaic||he arrived}}, {{cog|la|nancisci||to get}}, {{cog|sq|kënaq||to please, satisfy}}).

